Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Matter contributions to the graviton self-energy", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ea18b485-5df7-449e-bfba-4f4444571a35"],

Cell["\<\
Explore scalar, Dirac fermion, massive-vector, massless-vector and SU(N) \
matter contributions. Each sector constructs tadpole and bubble terms, forms \
their stated sum, and examines its tensor structure.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0913169-f191-495c-a02a-a20241999d3f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"36e4b7e4-c248-4ad6-bd93-3b8eac7e68e0"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"343a6c8b-f813-467f-8277-ead69bf1c5c8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{4.00009664861095*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"efb5c4a7-7a16-4360-8fe4-80d12cda7a98"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook requires FORM on the kernel\[CloseCurlyQuote]s PATH. \
CalcFormCalculate performs bosonic algebra and Lorentz contractions; TFORM is \
used automatically when available. FeynCalc handles loop reduction and any \
Dirac or colour algebra before the bosonic coefficients are sent to FORM.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2fc4fc2-bd9d-46fd-a918-254cbdb6ed2b"],

Cell["\<\
Explicit expands FeynCalc propagator shorthand before export. SUNSimplify \
contracts colour indices, and DiracSimplify with DiracOrder -> True reduces \
and orders open Dirac chains. Collect sends only the bosonic coefficients of \
the remaining DiracGamma or SUNDelta structures to CalcFormCalculate. Loop \
reduction stays in FeynCalc. SUNNToCACF -> False keeps colour factors in terms \
of SUNN, matching the displayed reference formulas.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"85a7c34b-9a5b-4e00-bbae-7307cc38f0a5"],

Cell["\<\
The external momentum is p, the loop momentum is k, and m denotes the matter \
mass where present. Repeated Lorentz or colour indices are summed. TID[..., k, \
ToPaVe -> True] reduces tensor integrals to scalar A0 and B0 functions. In \
FeynCalc\[CloseCurlyQuote]s convention these expressions retain the i \[Pi]\
\.b2 normalisation; no (2\[Pi])^(-D) loop-measure prefactor is inserted here. \
Keep D symbolic during reduction. Setting D -> 4 in a displayed coefficient \
is not a Laurent expansion, UV subtraction, or a renormalised answer.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd20420e-ebd5-4b06-b425-8bb3fca8108a"],

Cell["\<\
FeynGrav supplies the vertex and propagator normalisations, including i and \
\[Kappa]. The default gravitational gauge parameter is GaugeFixingEpsilon = \
2. The displayed diagram weights are retained from the original example; the \
notebook does not derive their combinatorics.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf167e0d-22aa-4c9b-8652-0ffba68fac81"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"importSUNYM", "[", "2", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7dd18be5-e2f1-4515-bdfc-16cc8969eead"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2. Scalar loop", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a675ab2f-13f8-4433-9d48-03baf33868c8"],

Cell["\<\
Use the stored diagram functions to inspect this sector independently after \
setup. The massless-vector and Yang\[Dash]Mills sections include the \
displayed ghost terms. Fermion chains use Dot and DiracTrace, retaining their \
order. GravitonFermionVertex takes graviton triples {index, index, incoming \
momentum}; include these momenta even when older examples list only the \
indices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4be0008-af09-4c29-a1d1-282749f2defd"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tadpole contributions", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"026a4747-0581-4696-bdb0-4867adc472d2"],

Cell["\<\
Close two matter legs of a contact vertex into a loop. A massive tadpole can \
contribute A0[m\.b2]; do not discard it as scaleless.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"aac256ff-ee4e-41b1-9a45-1667e37b7f08"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar1", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]"}], 
          "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "k", ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"ScalarPropagator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"k", ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000096722250681*^9, 4.0000967727344418`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fcb3f4af-fdb3-4c90-9a8a-9851213688b3"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bubble contributions", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"16f792aa-3dda-4469-80d2-8a10c2643304"],

Cell["\<\
Join the two matter\[Dash]graviton vertices with the indicated propagators. \
The integrand specifies the momentum routing; k is the integration variable.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd9438dc-d1c5-486c-8291-a562a1ef0f61"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar2", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "}"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"GravitonScalarVertex", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]"}], "}"}], ",", "k", ",", 
         RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"ScalarPropagator", "[", 
        RowBox[{"k", ",", "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"ScalarPropagator", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"p", "-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0000967770324097`*^9, 4.000096806945573*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f51acc98-6240-4100-ad7d-1a608a7ad188"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Combined tensor", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b373bbc9-5b5f-4035-84d4-440408cb0225"],

Cell["\<\
Add the stored terms with the weights written here and collect scalar \
integral coefficients. These are amputated tensors in this example\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s convention.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b765e80c-95a3-4319-9fa9-f3236e274110"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar1", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar2", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "Factor"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7f47ccc6-ab17-4abc-8b2a-19ae04a18104"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Longitudinal contractions", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"89112d24-b8a4-4a0a-aaf5-f00f634aefde"],

Cell["\<\
Inspect the contraction with the external momentum. A zero residual means \
that this particular contraction vanishes. Off-shell or massive-sector \
residuals should be read as displayed; this cell alone does not establish a \
full renormalised Ward identity.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4a52c016-3252-4280-81d5-113bd5528b89"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
       "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FVD", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "\[Mu]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "==", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0000966825577087`*^9, 4.000096684102426*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"988c5c68-86bc-4d9c-ae50-90fd876ddfe2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
       "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FVD", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "\[Nu]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "==", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0000968322034483`*^9, 4.000096840978086*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"09693954-e018-4ae4-927b-dab4380921b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
       "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FVD", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "\[Alpha]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "==", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000096834107339*^9, 4.00009684346579*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1bc376cc-98cd-4469-a245-7a11e1d6a624"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
   RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
       "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"FVD", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "\[Beta]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], "==", 
  "0"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000096838070822*^9, 4.00009684650417*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d8ab6824-5ccb-4422-862a-a229aca5285d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Projector form and comparison", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b021786c-7928-48a4-8998-00e387b5dbdc"],

Cell["\<\
Store the computed and reference tensors under explicit names, display the \
reference, and compare them after the stated D -> 4 substitution. True means \
agreement; an unevaluated equality is unresolved, not a successful check.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3908227a-e298-41f8-9dce-46234ca8323f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"scalarComputed", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit", "[", 
     RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorScalar", "[", 
      RowBox[{
      "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
       "m"}], "]"}], "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[10]:=",ExpressionUUID->"fd652b1c-8a73-4984-a16f-8375d0886945"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"scalarReference", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", "2"], " ", "\[ImaginaryI]", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"B0", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
          RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], ",", 
         SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], ",", 
         SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox["1", "12"], " ", 
          SuperscriptBox[
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
              RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], "+", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", 
              SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}]}], ")"}], "2"], " ", 
          RowBox[{"NieuwenhuizenOperator0", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}],
            "]"}]}], "+", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox["1", "120"], " ", 
          SuperscriptBox[
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
              RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], "-", 
             RowBox[{"4", " ", 
              SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}]}], ")"}], "2"], " ", 
          RowBox[{"NieuwenhuizenOperator2", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}],
            "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}], "-", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Kappa]", "2"], " ", "\[ImaginaryI]", " ", 
       SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"A0", "[", 
        SuperscriptBox["m", "2"], "]"}], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox["1", "6"], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
             RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], "+", 
            RowBox[{"2", " ", 
             SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"NieuwenhuizenOperator0", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}],
            "]"}]}], "+", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox["1", "60"], " ", 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"SP", "[", 
             RowBox[{"p", ",", "p"}], "]"}], "+", 
            RowBox[{"8", " ", 
             SuperscriptBox["m", "2"]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
          RowBox[{"NieuwenhuizenOperator2", "[", 
           RowBox[{
           "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}],
            "]"}]}]}], ")"}]}]}], "]"}], "/.", "\[VeryThinSpace]", 
    RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[11]:=",ExpressionUUID->"ad5c0ec4-365a-44b3-a653-6f8b005962cb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
  RowBox[{"scalarComputed", "\[Equal]", "scalarReference"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000096883683794*^9, 4.000096890151473*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[12]:=",ExpressionUUID->"e5e809cf-ddd2-4db9-993a-549edf31edd7"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Dirac fermion loop", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c99f528a-187e-4dd4-8dac-ff3e634e0502"],

Cell["\<\
Use the stored diagram functions to inspect this sector independently after \
setup. The massless-vector and Yang\[Dash]Mills sections include the \
displayed ghost terms. Fermion chains use Dot and DiracTrace, retaining their \
order. GravitonFermionVertex takes graviton triples {index, index, incoming \
momentum}; include these momenta even when older examples list only the \
indices.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68e96355-4f67-416f-a734-c742d9d2393c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tadpole contributions", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d193e724-b597-44f8-9499-a623c11bfd93"],

Cell["\<\
Close two matter legs of a contact vertex into a loop. A massive tadpole can \
contribute A0[m\.b2]; do not discard it as scaleless.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c905082d-07d2-46ff-96b4-2e3d8451e249"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion1", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"DiracTrace", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
            "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", 
             ",", 
             RowBox[{"-", "p"}]}], "}"}], ",", "k", ",", 
           RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
         RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"k", ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "//", 
      "Explicit"}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000096899381507*^9, 4.000096899626433*^9}, {
  4.000097454156126*^9, 4.0000975084922*^9}, {4.000097661787676*^9, 
  4.000097665384454*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[13]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f9d98ece-554e-49e6-9832-16c1fd32ef07"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bubble contributions", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"25975c49-5b57-4bd3-a721-e8c9ff0a7476"],

Cell["\<\
Join the two matter\[Dash]graviton vertices with the indicated propagators. \
The integrand specifies the momentum routing; k is the integration variable.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6c58ee4-3cae-4213-b2db-826757650c03"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion2", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"TID", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       RowBox[{"DiracTrace", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p"}], "}"}], ",", "k", ",", 
           RowBox[{"-", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"p", "+", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
         RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"k", ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}], ".", 
         RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
             RowBox[{"-", "p"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"p", "+", "k"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
         RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"p", "+", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "//",
       "Explicit"}], ",", "k", ",", 
     RowBox[{"ToPaVe", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000097517226603*^9, 4.000097558271748*^9}, {
   4.000097628472246*^9, 4.000097639678172*^9}, 4.0000976699001493`*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[14]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aafaf6c7-3a6e-408c-a227-6c5ebf993c2d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Combined tensor", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d830ff05-6f20-470a-8bd0-58d7da9db280"],

Cell["\<\
Add the stored terms with the weights written here and collect scalar \
integral coefficients. These are amputated tensors in this example\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s convention.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ea7b7aea-ab78-4f57-9d6e-bbbc0752c367"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion1", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion2", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#1", ",", "m", ",", "Factor"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[15]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a05e6ff7-20c3-4882-85d6-947379b6875a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Longitudinal contractions", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"5bde6420-2bdc-4775-a040-eb9feee913b0"],

Cell["\<\
Inspect the contraction with the external momentum. A zero residual means \
that this particular contraction vanishes. Off-shell or massive-sector \
residuals should be read as displayed; this cell alone does not establish a \
full renormalised Ward identity.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1f7b6032-98bc-4d1b-83c5-03843a958d65"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Pair", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Momentum", "[", 
      RowBox[{"p", ",", "D"}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"Momentum", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Polarization", "[", 
        RowBox[{"p", ",", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], "]"}], ",", "D"}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}], "=", "0"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[16]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d04c65e5-484b-4565-b0a9-0ab4ebba8af9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"FVD", "[", 
       RowBox[{"p", ",", "\[Mu]"}], "]"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"PolarizationTensor", "[", 
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], "]"}], 
   ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "Factor"}], "]"}]], "Input",\

 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[17]:=",ExpressionUUID->"29e10226-6dde-4f1b-9e48-c765dde0df13"],

